    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">30 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip accent\">HLD Pattern</span>\n          <span class=\"chip kafka\">Kafka</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Meta</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>Pattern: Counting, Ranking &amp; Windowed Aggregation</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">\"How many?\" sounds like the easiest question in computing, until it is asked a million times a second about a billion things. After this page you can design counters, per-minute aggregates, unique counts and top-K lists that are fast, cheap and correct enough - and say exactly how correct.</p>\n      "
